**My own answer:**

The user wants a "flip card" effect: by default, only the image is visible; on hover, the card rotates, the image becomes blurred, and the `.info` div appears on the back of the card. The current structure doesn't allow this because `.info` is always visible and not positioned as a back face.

**Correct approach:**
- Use a wrapper (`.carte-inner`) inside `.carte` for the 3D rotation.
- Have two faces: front (image) and back (`.info`).
- Use `backface-visibility: hidden` and `transform-style: preserve-3d`.
- On hover, rotate `.carte-inner` by 180deg on Y axis.
- Blur the image on hover for extra effect.

**Example HTML:**
```html
<div class="carte">
  <div class="carte-inner">
    <div class="carte-face carte-front">
      <img src="./images/rootme_logo.svg" alt="Logo du site RootMe">
    </div>
    <div class="carte-face carte-back">
      <div class="info">Root Me</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

**Example CSS:**
```css
.carte {
  width: 200px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;
}

.carte-inner {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transition: transform 0.6s;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;
}

.carte:hover .carte-inner {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

.carte-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border: 1px solid var(--accent-color);
  border-radius: 5px;
  background: var(--secondary-color);
}

.carte-front img {
  max-width: 50%;
  transition: filter 0.3s;
}

.carte:hover .carte-front img {
  filter: blur(3px);
}

.carte-back {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: var(--accent-color);
}
```

**Explanation:**
- `.carte-inner` rotates on hover, flipping the card.
- `.carte-front` is the image, `.carte-back` is the info.
- Only one face is visible at a time.
- The image blurs on hover.

