   struct Node {
       std::array<Node*, 26> children;
       int cnt;
       Node() : cnt(0) {
           children.fill(nullptr);
       }
   };
   ```

2. **Use a map/unordered_map for sparse tries:**  
   If your trie is very sparse (most nodes have few children), you can use `std::unordered_map<char, Node*>` for children. This saves memory at the cost of slower access.

   ```cpp
