The main issue is that your script defines a function (`loadAndModifySVG`) to fetch and modify the SVG, but in the DOMContentLoaded event, you are not using it—instead, you fetch and insert the SVG without modification. Also, your replacement string in the regex uses single quotes inside single quotes, which can cause issues.

Here’s how you can fix your `fetch_svg.js`:

```js
// fetch_svg.js

// Function to load and modify SVG content
function loadAndModifySVG(url, callback) {
  fetch(url)
    .then(response => {
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Network response was not ok');
      return response.text();
